Stop splitting a line at its last field when no blank follows it.
Without -t, join stepped past the line's terminator. A line read with
its newline happens to have a second terminator after the first, but an
unterminated last line does not, so join read past its end and printed
garbage as extra fields.

---
 coreutils/join.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/coreutils/join.c
+++ b/coreutils/join.c
@@ -118,6 +118,8 @@
 
 		sl[n] = s;
 		n++;
+		if (s1 == NULL)
+			break;  /* don't step past the terminator */
 		s += sn + 1;
 	}
 	curr->fieldcount = n;
